# Conventional Commits

## Subject Line

Format: `{type}({scope}): {description}`

| Type | Use For |
|------|---------|
| feat | New feature |
| fix | Bug fix |
| test | Adding/updating tests |
| refactor | Code restructuring (no behaviour change) |
| docs | Documentation only |
| chore | Build, config, dependencies |
| perf | Performance improvement |

## Full Format (Agent Commits)

```
{type}({scope}): {description}

{optional body}

Tasks: {task-ids}
Agent-Session: tool={tool} model={model} agents={agent-ids} tokens={in}K/{out}K duration={time}

Co-Authored-By: {tool-or-model} <email>
```

## Agent-Session Line (triplet)

Machine-parseable. **Record the triplet accurately: tool, model, agent(s).**

| Field | Format | Example |
|-------|--------|---------|
| tool | IDE/platform that ran the model | tool=cursor, tool=claude-ide, tool=copilot |
| model | Model/backend used | model=sonnet, model=opus, model=gpt-4 |
| agents | Agent(s) from context/agents | agents=python-coder, agents=functional-tester,code-reviewer |
| tokens | in/out with K suffix | tokens=12.4K/8.2K |
| duration | minutes or hours | duration=45m |

Agent names come from `context/agents/*.md`. Use the actual (tool, model, agent) for the commit; do not substitute a default.

## Examples

### Agent Commit

```
feat(auth): add token refresh endpoint

Tasks: AUTH-001
Agent-Session: tool=cursor model=sonnet agents=python-coder tokens=8.2K/5.1K duration=32m

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>
```

### Human Commit

```
docs(api): update OpenAPI spec for backtest endpoint

Tasks: DOC-001
```

## Rules

- Max 72 chars for subject line
- Scope matches service/component name
- Description is imperative ("add" not "added")
- Tasks line references tasks.md
- Agent commits require Agent-Session and Co-Authored-By

Full template: `templates/commit-message.template.md`
